---
import Layout from "../../Base.astro";
import SimpleHero from "../../components/SimpleHero.astro";
import FeaturedArticles from "../../components/FeaturedArticles.astro";
import ServicesRelatedWork from "../../components/ServicesRelatedWork.astro";
import "../../styles/pages/_services-list.scss";
---

<Layout
  title="Paid Search &amp; Social Campaign Management | Kelp"
  description="Paid search and social campaigns built around qualified results, strong creative, useful landing pages, and clear measurement."
>
  <SimpleHero
    tagline="Digital Marketing Services"
    title="Social & PPC"
    description="Paid campaigns only work when the targeting, creative, and landing experience support the same goal. We manage social and PPC campaigns that put the right message in front of the right people at the right time."
    lottieFile="social-media-content.json"
  />
  <div class="service-body">
    <div class="wrapper wrapper--narrow">
      <h2>Where teams get stuck</h2>
      <p>
        Paid media gets expensive fast when clicks are arriving but the
        campaigns are not producing meaningful movement. In most cases, the
        problem is not the platform alone. It is the mismatch between targeting,
        creative, offer, and landing experience.
      </p>
      <p>
        That is why some businesses keep spending more while learning very
        little.
      </p>
      <h2>How we fix it</h2>
      <p>
        We treat paid media like a system. Audience strategy, campaign
        structure, creative direction, testing, and reporting all need to
        support the same outcome so the spend has a real chance to perform.
      </p>
      <h2>Platforms we work with</h2>
      <ul>
        <li>Facebook</li>
        <li>Twitter</li>
        <li>Instagram</li>
        <li>LinkedIn</li>
        <li>Google Ads</li>
      </ul>
      <h2>Start with the Buying Question</h2>
      <p>
        Search ads can reach people already looking for a solution. Social
        campaigns can introduce an offer or bring previous visitors back. We
        choose the channel based on the audience and the decision, then align
        the ad with a page that continues the same conversation.
      </p>
      <h2>Measure What Matters After the Click</h2>
      <p>
        We review search terms or audience signals, spend, conversion paths, and
        lead quality. If traffic is relevant but actions are weak, the landing
        page may need work. If leads arrive but do not fit, the offer or
        targeting may be wrong. Our <a href="/work/elev8-fun/">Elev8 Fun</a> work combined paid social with
        design, campaigns, web development, and ongoing support.
      </p>
      <p>
        Before increasing spend, scan your landing site with Kelp's free{" "}
        <a href="/website-checker/">Website Checker</a> and test the actual
        enquiry or checkout path. Plan a campaign with Kelp.
      </p>
      <h2>How This Works in Practice</h2>
      <p>
        Search and social play different roles. Search captures an expressed
        need, while social can introduce a useful idea before a customer starts
        looking. The mix depends on the offer, buying cycle, and quality of
        available creative. We also plan exclusions, location settings, and
        destination pages so budget is not spent bringing the wrong visitor to
        an unclear next step.
      </p>
      <h2>What the Work Includes</h2>
      <ul>
        <li>Campaign structure and audience or query plan</li>
        <li>Ad copy and creative direction matched to landing pages</li>
        <li>Conversion tracking and lead-quality review</li>
        <li>Ongoing adjustments informed by real results</li>
      </ul>
      <h2>What Moving Forward Looks Like</h2>
      <p>
        A useful first conversation includes the current campaigns, landing
        pages, budget, and a few examples of good and poor leads. We can
        identify the most likely source of waste and agree on what to change
        first.
      </p>
      <h2>Frequently Asked Questions</h2>
      <h3>How do we know whether a campaign is working?</h3>
      <p>
        We compare spend with qualified enquiries or sales, then inspect the
        path between the ad and that outcome. Click-through rate alone cannot
        answer the business question.
      </p>
      <p>
        <a href="/contact/" class="button button--green">
          Review Your Paid Strategy
        </a>
      </p>
    </div>
    <ServicesRelatedWork tag={86} />
  </div>
  <FeaturedArticles />
</Layout>
